{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"fungoid-inanimate-cornsnake","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# Where the unsigned events come from\n\nThe project intends to sign every event, but ~11.2k ACTIVE events carry no `author_sig`.\nBroken down by `env_id`, the cause is NOT diffuse — it is one environment.\n\n## Evidence — signed rate per environment (active, non-SNAPSHOT events)\n\n| env_id | signed | unsigned | signed% | last seen | top author |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| b2b5c498 | 0 | 8880 | 0.0% | 2026-08-09T16:16 | Unknown (8880) |\n| ade0f2ef (this host) | 9617 | 2186 | 81.5% | 2026-08-09T18:22 | RebarBotNava |\n| reconciler | 95 | 93 | 50.5% | 2026-08-07 | reconciler |\n| 4d084713 | 243 | 0 | 100% | 2026-08-08 | RebarBotNava |\n| rebar-bridge[bot] envs | 10 | 0 | 100% | — | rebar-bridge[bot] |\n\n**env b2b5c498 is the problem**: 8880 events, ZERO signed, every one authored \"Unknown\",\nand still writing. Its envelopes carry `author: \"Unknown\"`, `author_id: null`,\n`author_email: \"\"`, `author_sig: null`, `creation_channel: null` — i.e. NO identity is\nconfigured in that environment at all, so both the authorship stamp and the signature are\nskipped, and the creation-channel provenance feature is also a no-op there.\n\nIt is GROWING: 2818 events in 2026-07, 6062 in 2026-08.\n\nEvent types it writes: CLAIM_ENRICH 1500, TICKET_DIGEST 1496, DONE_ENRICH 1496,\nREVIEW_RESULT 1187, CREATE 1185, LINK 1100, ENQUEUE_ENRICH 912, COMMENT 4. First seen\n2026-07-10 20:58, right after the event-sourced enrichment queue landed (75d1a4672d,\n2026-07-09) — so it looks like a headless drainer/automation environment. Note it also\nCREATEs tickets and writes REVIEW_RESULTs unsigned, so the gap is not limited to the\nenrichment queue.\n\n## This host is NOT the problem\nade0f2ef's 2186 unsigned events are legacy: 772 from 2026-06, 1412 from 2026-07, and only\n**2** in 2026-08. Signing works here now. Store-wide the June rate was 0% signed (the feature\ndid not exist), July 51%, August 48% — and the August figure is dragged down almost entirely\nby b2b5c498.\n\n## Not to be confused with the b636 restore\nThe b636 remediation restored 5041 unsigned historical events, which moved fsck's raw tally.\nThat was benign (they predate signing). THIS ticket is the separate, ongoing gap.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Identify the host/process behind env_id b2b5c498 (its events are the only lead:\n      enrichment-queue drainer + CREATE/LINK/REVIEW_RESULT, first seen 2026-07-10).\n- [ ] That environment writes events with a resolved author identity AND an `author_sig`.\n- [ ] `creation_channel` is stamped there too (currently null for all 8880).\n- [ ] A guard makes an identity-less writer loud rather than silent — e.g. the append path\n      refuses, or fsck reports an env whose signed-rate is 0%, so this cannot recur unnoticed.\n- [ ] Decide the disposition of the 8880 existing unsigned events (backfill is likely\n      impossible — signatures cannot be forged retroactively; document them as an accepted\n      pre-fix cohort scoped out of verify-authorship).","id":"beb1-d778-e7d9-425a","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"One environment writes every event unsigned and identity-less (author=Unknown, 8880 events, ongoing)"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786300111515176001,"uuid":"73b4975b-5df7-4b89-94f7-91271e23b037"}